  "about": {
    "eyebrow": "About",
    "title": "A shop run by <em>anglers</em>.",
    "lede": "Based in Perpignan since 2008, we curate every product with the same question in mind: would we enjoy fishing with it?",
    "cta": "See the shop",
    "history": {
      "eyebrow": "Since 2008",
      "title": "Our story",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Hook &amp; Cook opened in 2008 in a small shop on rue de l'Alsace in Perpignan. Back then: a counter, three fly rods hanging on the wall, and a box of flies hand-tied by Jean-Marc Peyre, a former guide on the Têt river.",
        "Eighteen years later, the shop has grown and the catalogue covers every technique — fly, predator, surfcasting, carp — but the approach stays the same: pick every product as if we were going to fish with it ourselves. No algorithmic catalogue, no anonymous Asian supplier. Rods we cast, reels we strip down, lures we test on the Têt before they hit the shelf.",
        "Today the team is five anglers. We organise three or four contests a year on local waters (Têt, Vinça, Tech, Agly), we coach beginners, and we still tie our own flies in the shop on winter mornings."
      ]
    },
    "workshops": {
      "eyebrow": "Made in France",
      "title": "Partner workshops",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Part of our range is produced directly by French workshops we work with in direct trade, no middlemen. It guarantees quality, traceability, and keeps local artisan know-how alive."
      ],
      "list": [
        "<strong>Atelier Peyre (66)</strong> — Jean-Marc hand-mounts the carbon blanks of the Hook &amp; Cook Sauvage range in Prades. Walnut-turned reel seats, silk-thread guides. Half a dozen rods a month.",
        "<strong>Cordier Roubinet (38)</strong> — one of the last French rope makers to weave their fly lines by hand on a hundred-year-old loom. 16-strand core, beeswax finishing.",
        "<strong>Tournon (42)</strong> — historic French manufacturer of hooks and fine accessories. Made in the Loire region, zinc-plated steel, black finish.",
